Mechanism
crates/bbt-mux/src/seat_socket.rs — after the existing authorized/journaled GUI mute succeeds, read the authoritative GuiSeat and send it before the existing Messaging receipt. Only the GUI door receives that snapshot. The ctl response shape and native mutation authorization are unchanged. The retained state event and its ACK still flow through the bus independently.
crates/bboxy450-term/src/live.rs — the existing FIFO classifier keeps a raw Seat snapshot separate from the correlated Messaging receipt; its new pure regression covers an outstanding mute followed by ordinary input.
scripts/night-boundaries.d/bbt-mux.sh — exact selector for the real supervisor/PTY/socket regression. That boundary is night-only. No operator identity, login Keychain, window or desktop input is used.
The app's three-second UI receipt deadline is unchanged. No assertion is relaxed.

Deterministic counterexample
The real socket test never attaches an events lane. On the old implementation the mute operation receipt arrives before any authoritative state and the test fails. After the fix GUI mute, unmute and a repeated same-value write all expose retained metadata first; ctl retains its old single terminal reply.
The before/after timeout is a 30-second hang guard, not a speed assertion. The protocol order and retained metadata determine the verdict.

